1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:11,011
[in Korean] I like you.

4
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:44,920
EPISODE 5

5
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:07,067
[in English] Oh, why are you so heavy?

6
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:13,240
Why did you have to eat 20 pounds
of food for dinner?

7
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:14,658
I didn't eat that much food!

8
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:18,829
-[chuckles] Oh, you're awake?
-If I'm so heavy, then put me down.

9
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,582
-[in Korean] Okay, okay.
-[in English] Put me down. Let go of me.

10
00:01:21,665 --> 00:01:24,084
-Drop me. Hey.
-[in Korean] Okay!

11
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:25,419
-[giggles]
-[chuckles]

12
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:27,254
[in English] Are you okay?

13
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:29,089
-[in Korean] You all right?
-I'm not all right.

14
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:31,091
Wow, your Korean's getting better.

15
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:34,177
[chuckles] Mmm.

16
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:40,058
-Star.
-Star.

17
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:42,728
-Moon.
-Moon.

18
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,856
-Sky.
-Sky. [chuckles]

19
00:01:48,734 --> 00:01:50,444
-Love.
-Love.

20
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:53,822
-Yubin. [chuckles]
-Yubin.

21
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:58,327
You know really beautiful words.

22
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:00,787
Your turn. I'll test you.

23
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:01,913
-Test me?
-Mm-hmm.

24
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:03,540
Uh…

25
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:06,126
-Strawberry.
-Wow.

26
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,420
-Robber.
-Hmm? [chuckles]

27
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,756
-Airhead.
-Airhead?

28
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:11,840
Dummy.

29
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:14,593
-[chuckling] What the heck?
-[laughing]

30
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:17,929
-Star.
-Mm-hmm.

31
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:20,057
-Moon.
-Mm-hmm.

32
00:02:21,183 --> 00:02:22,768
-Sky.
-Mm-hmm.

33
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:24,978
Love.

34
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,148
Karin.

35
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:56,385
DEAR KARIN

36
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:38,969
Why does Kunam always have to
take things so seriously?

37
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:43,348
-Your pronunciation's on point.
-[chuckling]

38
00:03:43,432 --> 00:03:46,476
One for you. Here you are.
Thanks for visiting us.

39
00:03:55,819 --> 00:03:59,156
Hey there, you here all by yourself?
Wanna drink with the two of us?

40
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,950
-No, thanks. I'm here with someone.
-[scoffs] Doubt that.

41
00:04:02,451 --> 00:04:03,952
You've been here a whole hour

42
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:06,037
-drinking by yourself.
-I told you guys I'm not here alone.

43
00:04:06,121 --> 00:04:08,623
-Yeah, whatever. Sounds good.
-Chill out and drink with us.

44
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,625
A toast to us.

45
00:04:10,709 --> 00:04:12,419
-Cheers. [chuckles]
-Cheers.

46
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:18,884
You're in my seat.
And you're talking to my girlfriend.

47
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:23,138
-Really, dude?
-Ah, man, I guess she's got a boyfriend.

48
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,931
-Our bad. Yeah, sorry.
-Hey. Sorry about that.

49
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,523
Since when have you started
calling me your girlfriend?

50
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:35,442
Okay. Is calling you my boyfriend better?

51
00:04:38,904 --> 00:04:40,530
How did you know that I was here?

52
00:04:42,741 --> 00:04:46,953
By manner of deduction.
I checked all the food stalls, one by one.

53
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:49,206
#LONELY NIGHT - #FUKUOKA
#FOOD STAND

54
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,922
I can't believe you.

55
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:03,678
Mari, are you…

56
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:08,725
interested in me even a little?

57
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:15,899
When I confessed my feelings, I…

58
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,736
I wasn't joking around or anything.

59
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:26,660
I meant what I said before.

60
00:05:29,538 --> 00:05:31,164
I've always been serious about you.

61
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:38,046
Why do you always have to
be so heavy about this?

62
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,507
Like I said before,

63
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,843
I just want to play and have fun.

64
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,179
I don't mind, Mari,
you can have fun.

65
00:05:47,097 --> 00:05:48,306
Let me be…

66
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,433
the serious one.

67
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:54,062
Do you think you can…

68
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:56,648
give us a chance?

69
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:01,903
Mari, you're here.

70
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:05,198
A winning prize for Charo
will make you happy, Mari.

71
00:06:05,282 --> 00:06:10,036
I really… Mari, I really like you a lot.

72
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:33,435
When we're done with these drinks,
that's when our relationship will begin.

73
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:48,783
-[sighs, chuckles]
-[chuckles]

74
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:01,713
Mari, wait. Is… is this real?

75
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:24,152
It hurts all over.

76
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,946
I overdid it last night.

77
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:29,824
You shocked me with how much strength
you have, you know that?

78
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:34,037
Well, I guess I'm more vigorous
than I thought.

79
00:07:37,749 --> 00:07:40,543
You're the reason
everything hurts so much!

80
00:07:46,758 --> 00:07:48,343
Hey, Mari, listen…

81
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:50,804
Tonight I'm gonna…

82
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:53,807
I'm gonna protect you.

83
00:07:57,602 --> 00:08:00,939
Whatever. What are you protecting me from?

84
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:03,983
It's the other way around.

85
00:08:05,819 --> 00:08:07,445
-[grunting]
-[groaning]

86
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:09,781
Mari.

87
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:16,204
[in English] I… I have no idea
what you're saying. [exclaims]

88
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:19,958
I'm sorry if I was annoying.

89
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:21,376
I'm kind of a lightweight with alcohol.

90
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:22,460
Mm-hmm.

91
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:26,798
Hey, by the way, what does
"Nan neo-bak-ae-oep-seo" mean?

92
00:08:27,966 --> 00:08:29,551
It means, "You're my one and only."

93
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:33,596
All right. Keep massaging with vigor.

94
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,848
Aye-aye.

95
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:36,224
-Right here?
-Mm-hmm.

96
00:08:44,107 --> 00:08:46,234
-[door opens]
-[footsteps approaching]

97
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:54,284
-[knocks]
-Oh. [chuckles]

98
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:55,910
What are you doing over there?

99
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:56,995
Ah.

100
00:08:58,121 --> 00:08:59,456
-Coffee.
-Ah.

101
00:09:14,137 --> 00:09:15,138
DEAR KARIN

102
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:31,613
What kind of relationship do we have?

103
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:44,125
Korea… Dating… Start dating…

104
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,252
What to know.

105
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:52,550
Huh?

106
00:09:52,634 --> 00:09:54,761
THE REAL KOREAN DATING CULTURE
DISPLAYING AFFECTION

107
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:57,639
"In Korea, there are steps before
becoming official." What's that mean?

108
00:09:57,722 --> 00:10:01,601
DATING STARTS WITH
AN AMBIGUOUS RELATIONSHIP

109
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:05,855
"The In-between phase is called… <i>Sseom</i>?"

110
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:13,446
"Don't be overly affectionate. Make sure
to keep the right amount of space."

111
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:20,453
How? We live together.

112
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:29,129
WHAT MAKES KOREAN MEN ATTRACTIVE
&amp; THE PROS OF DATING ONE

113
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:31,214
"Only be physical after you're official."

114
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:32,674
[gasps] Wait a minute.

115
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:39,264
Then are we…

116
00:10:39,806 --> 00:10:41,266
-[chief] Karin.
-Who's there?

117
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:42,684
[exclaims] Oh, Chief.

118
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,561
I'm sorry. Did I scare you?

119
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:46,187
It's all right. [grunts]

120
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:48,022
Can I help you with something?

121
00:10:48,106 --> 00:10:50,233
Actually, I came to ask a favor.

122
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,112
[in Korean] All right, this one…

123
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,698
And for dinner…

124
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,161
What should I make… Oh.

125
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:02,787
Karin! Karin. Karin.

126
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:04,914
-[in English] Huh?
-Want to take a break?

127
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:06,082
Hmm? What?

128
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:07,667
[in Korean] Hold on a sec.

129
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,627
[in English] Oh,
where-where are you going?

130
00:11:09,711 --> 00:11:12,130
-Out. The, uh… The Chief said that…
-Huh?

131
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:14,299
-a… a visitor has just arrived…
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Yes?

132
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:17,010
…and he wants me
to give them a tour of the village.

133
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:19,596
Oh. You want me to come with you?

134
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:24,976
THE RIGHT AMOUNT OF SPACE

135
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:28,354
No, no, no. Yubin, I need you here.

136
00:11:28,438 --> 00:11:30,398
-We have so much work to do here, right?
-Ah.

137
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:32,400
-Um, the bugs in the field…
-Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

138
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:34,819
-Oh, the bugs.
-Please pick them with your hands. Okay?

139
00:11:34,903 --> 00:11:36,237
-With my hands.
-Mm-hmm.

140
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,365
Ah. Oh, Karin!

141
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:42,577
You and I can have our dinner together?

142
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:46,706
Mm-hmm, sounds good. See you later then!

143
00:11:51,878 --> 00:11:55,006
I pick the bugs with my hands.
Pick the bugs every day, pick the bugs.

144
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,799
[in Korean] Well, then…

145
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,434
It's worn out.

146
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:10,313
How many times did someone bump into this

147
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,941
for it to look like this?

148
00:12:14,901 --> 00:12:16,110
Wait a minute…

149
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:25,912
CHARO VILLAGE OFFICE

150
00:12:31,668 --> 00:12:34,128
-Thank you for the ride. I appreciate it!
-[chief] Of course.

151
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:42,136
She mentioned that she was here
for some kinda resort planning business.

152
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:45,139
-A resort business?
-Mm-hmm.

153
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:48,017
She came all this way
and said she wanted to take a tour.

154
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:49,435
Ooh.

155
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:52,272
So thanks for showing her around.

156
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:54,732
-Of course.
-I can't do it because of this.

157
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,985
Seems to scare a lot of people off.

158
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,989
-Ah, I see. [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

159
00:13:01,072 --> 00:13:02,323
Happy to help.

160
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:04,117
Where should our first stop be?

161
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,702
Ah! We're over here!

162
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:23,886
-Hello there.
-Hi.

163
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,305
Hello there.

164
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:27,098
Are you my tour guide around the island?

165
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:30,143
Uh, yes. Shirahama Karin. It's a pleasure.

166
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:32,395
I'm Han Sia.

167
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,105
I flew here from Korea.

168
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:38,651
Ah. You can speak comfortably,
I'll understand you.

169
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:44,407
[in Korean] I can… speak… a little bit.

170
00:13:46,034 --> 00:13:49,912
[in English] Wow. Well then, where do you
suggest we begin my tour today?

171
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:53,332
Don't worry.
You can leave everything to me. [chuckles]

172
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,501
We'll be on our way then.

173
00:14:03,301 --> 00:14:05,344
[in Korean] What should I make?

174
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,856
There it is!

175
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:19,984
-[in English] Oh. Excuse me, ma'am.
-[chuckles] It's all right.

176
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:22,653
-It's all yours. You can have it.
-[chuckles] Oh, the meat is mine?

177
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:24,572
-Oh, thank you very much.
-Yeah.

178
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:26,365
This one? Or this one?

179
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:28,618
The slices are much thicker on that one.

180
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,536
-Oh.
-Mmm, go with that one.

181
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:32,163
-Oh?
-I'd say it really takes the cake.

182
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,457
-You like this? This one "takes the cake"?
-Mmm. It'll be the best.

183
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:39,337
I took this little alleyway
every morning to school and back

184
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,630
when I was a young student.

185
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:44,592
-Oh, Mr. Sato. Hi. [chuckles]
-Hey, Karin. [chuckles] Hi.

186
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:47,720
-I'm giving her a tour. [chuckles]
-[Mr. Sato] Mmm.

187
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:52,391
As you can see, the people of this island
are incredibly kind

188
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:54,936
-and supportive of each other.
-[shutter clicks]

189
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:59,732
This area is known
for its beautiful scenery.

190
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:01,984
In the summer,
people come to this popular spot

191
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:04,529
to enjoy the vibrant blue hue of the water
against the sky.

192
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:07,698
Our communities come together
to help and support each other

193
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:09,075
as we grow various crops.

194
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:10,785
What else?

195
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:13,079
Let's go to the next stop.

196
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:20,253
I can't tell if she's interested
in our island or not.

197
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:40,606
[in Korean] Mix it up real good.

198
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:44,986
That's done.

199
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:52,493
It's kind of bland… Let's see.
Where's the salt? I'll add a dash of salt.

200
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:01,502
What's that building over there?

201
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,964
Oh, that's the community center.

202
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:07,466
That's nice and central.

203
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:11,554
It'll make a great food court or a café.

204
00:16:13,598 --> 00:16:15,850
It's central to all who live here.

205
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:18,728
That's why it's our community center.

206
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:19,812
That's cool.

207
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:23,774
[in Korean] Just a bunch of old people…

208
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:32,283
So, why live in the middle of nowhere?

209
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:33,910
Isn't it suffocating to you?

210
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,120
No, not at all.

211
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:39,624
Quite the opposite actually.
Living here clears my mind.

212
00:16:41,459 --> 00:16:44,420
Aren't you lonely living here
when you're so young?

213
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:46,881
There's nobody to hang out with
and no clubs to go to.

214
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:54,347
Believe it or not,
there's a lot more here than you think.

215
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:59,060
It's only something you learn
the longer you spend time here.

216
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:02,480
Hmm… I'll just have
to take your word for it.

217
00:17:04,774 --> 00:17:08,027
There is actually one last place
that I'd like to check out.

218
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:10,321
Sure. Where's that?

219
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:13,491
According to this,
it should be right next to us.

220
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,785
Oh. It's right over there.

221
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:27,505
[in Korean] All right.

222
00:17:33,344 --> 00:17:34,887
Whew, all done.

223
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:38,224
Ah.

224
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:44,355
Now it's ready.

225
00:17:49,652 --> 00:17:50,653
[in English] Um, so…

226
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,114
This place is…

227
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:56,450
That's my house over there
and my farm is right here.

228
00:17:57,994 --> 00:18:00,162
[in Korean] No wonder Lee Yubin's
got his eye on this place.

229
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:05,793
[in English] Welcome back!

230
00:18:06,586 --> 00:18:07,753
Hi.

231
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:10,047
[in Korean] Is that you, Yubin?

232
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:15,886
What are you doing here?

233
00:18:21,601 --> 00:18:22,602
Oh. [sighs]

234
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,278
So he's living here?

235
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:42,705
He's still designing stuff.

236
00:18:55,009 --> 00:18:56,969
Something's changed.

237
00:19:03,601 --> 00:19:08,064
FIVE YEARS AGO

238
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:17,198
How many nights have you spent staying up?

239
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:19,784
How can I get any work done at home?

240
00:19:20,368 --> 00:19:21,369
Fair point.

241
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,831
[Yubin] Go home before me.

242
00:19:28,459 --> 00:19:31,462
Your designs are right up my alley.

243
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:33,631
Get out of here already.

244
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:36,759
Still not interested
in joining our company?

245
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,260
I'm not interested.

246
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:42,098
We can meet pretty much all your terms.

247
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:46,519
I want to design freely
without any meddling in my way.

248
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,355
Ugh. You're such a handful.

249
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:53,275
And I love that.

250
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:59,365
You're not making any sense.

251
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:01,325
Compared to before…

252
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,203
his designs have become warmer.

253
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:32,440
I heard you were negotiating.

254
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,943
But I had no idea you were boarding here.

255
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:41,115
I mean… It's not exactly boarding.

256
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:44,493
It just… worked out that way.

257
00:20:45,536 --> 00:20:47,955
What are you doing here?

258
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:49,749
I came here to help you out.

259
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:52,168
I'll buy that land off you.

260
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,086
My land?

261
00:20:55,838 --> 00:20:57,256
That's…

262
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:03,471
You said that you made us dinner?

263
00:21:12,438 --> 00:21:14,732
Are you sure it doesn't bother you
that I'm staying for dinner?

264
00:21:15,483 --> 00:21:16,567
Of course it doesn't.

265
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:19,862
Yubin, Sia's an acquaintance
of yours, right?

266
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:22,990
-[chuckles] You two are friends?
-[Yubin] Huh?

267
00:21:23,616 --> 00:21:25,534
Uh, um, the two of us are not.

268
00:21:25,618 --> 00:21:27,536
-She's my work--
-I had a crush on him.

269
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:31,957
I used to be madly in love with Yubin,
but it was one-sided.

270
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:36,253
You see, I'm the girl who has always
gotten whatever it is that I wanted.

271
00:21:36,337 --> 00:21:39,924
Unfortunately for me,
Yubin's the only exception to that.

272
00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:45,095
[in Korean] Did you say something weird?

273
00:21:45,179 --> 00:21:47,014
I was just telling the truth.

274
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:56,899
How long do you plan on staying here?

275
00:21:56,982 --> 00:21:58,859
I've got it handled.
Just eat your food and go.

276
00:22:05,074 --> 00:22:07,993
[in English] Listen, Karin,
this might be beyond your comprehension.

277
00:22:08,994 --> 00:22:13,374
Yubin isn't the type of person
who belongs somewhere like this.

278
00:22:14,625 --> 00:22:16,085
What do you…

279
00:22:16,919 --> 00:22:18,546
Wait, uh, ho-ho-hold on.

280
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:23,551
Karin, I'll… help her leave. Mmm.

281
00:22:23,634 --> 00:22:25,719
What? You mean now?

282
00:22:25,803 --> 00:22:27,346
Yes, I mean now.

283
00:22:27,429 --> 00:22:29,473
-[in Korean] Come on. Stand up.
-[Sia] Ugh, why?

284
00:22:29,557 --> 00:22:31,684
[in English] Thanks for the tour today.
It's been fun.

285
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:32,852
[in Korean] Out you go.

286
00:22:32,935 --> 00:22:35,187
[in English] Oh, uh. Back in a second.

287
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:46,365
[Mari] Hello. Welcome.

288
00:22:48,409 --> 00:22:49,827
[in Korean] What a gaudy shop.

289
00:22:52,997 --> 00:22:54,707
We'll have two draft beers, please.

290
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:55,791
[Mari] Sure.

291
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:03,591
I'll cut right to the chase.

292
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:07,261
I'm not selling that property.

293
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:10,389
Then what's your plan?

294
00:23:13,976 --> 00:23:15,978
Are you willing to give up your career?

295
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,690
[in English] Please enjoy your drinks.

296
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:30,159
[in Korean] Just sell it off to me.

297
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:32,453
I'll buy it from you.

298
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:35,205
Just sell it off

299
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,042
and come back to Korea with me.

300
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:41,503
You need the money
to get back on your own feet.

301
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:42,922
That's none of your business.

302
00:23:43,005 --> 00:23:46,967
I can't let my senior's talent go to waste
in a place like this.

303
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:49,011
I'd hate to see that.

304
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:03,984
Mari, hi. Done with work already?

305
00:24:04,068 --> 00:24:05,986
I couldn't breathe in there.
I had to leave.

306
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:08,614
I seriously thought
I was going to pass out or something.

307
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:10,491
-Did something happen?
-Yeah. Yubin.

308
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:13,160
-He suddenly showed up with a weird woman.
-A weird woman?

309
00:24:13,243 --> 00:24:15,329
And their intense vibe was something else!

310
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:17,122
-Like our vibe is?
-How can you joke around

311
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:18,540
at a time like this?

312
00:24:18,624 --> 00:24:20,334
There's definitely something wrong.

313
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:22,294
The energy felt so off and dark.

314
00:24:22,878 --> 00:24:24,755
Almost as if she's his…

315
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:27,716
-[gasps] …his ex-girlfriend!
-His loan shark!

316
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:28,884
-What?
-Huh?

317
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:33,222
When he got here,
Yubin said he lost all his money.

318
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:34,848
That's gotta be why she's here.

319
00:24:34,932 --> 00:24:36,308
She's collecting her cash.

320
00:24:36,392 --> 00:24:38,978
You didn't see them.
That definitely can't be it.

321
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,855
[groans] What should I do?

322
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:45,693
I got it!
Kunam, keep an eye on them, okay?

323
00:24:45,776 --> 00:24:47,152
Oh, wait!

324
00:24:47,236 --> 00:24:50,280
If she tries to leave or anything,
run over there and make sure she pays.

325
00:24:50,364 --> 00:24:51,573
You got it.

326
00:25:00,374 --> 00:25:02,960
Wasn't he helping her leave?
Where the heck did he go?

327
00:25:03,711 --> 00:25:05,087
The ferry terminal?

328
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,755
[scoffs] Or the airport?

329
00:25:07,423 --> 00:25:09,633
Wait a minute,
he couldn't have gone to Korea…

330
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:13,137
What's Yubin doing?

331
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:16,056
He said he'd be back in a second.
It's been longer than that.

332
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,892
Karin. Karin? Karin!

333
00:25:18,976 --> 00:25:21,061
-Karin, Karin, hey… Karin.
-Oh, Mari…

334
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:22,688
-There's something I have to share.
-Huh?

335
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:23,897
Hurry. [stuttering]

336
00:25:23,981 --> 00:25:25,816
-Hurry and finish washing so we can talk.
-What?

337
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:28,610
A crush on Yubin?

338
00:25:28,694 --> 00:25:30,154
She said that to your face?

339
00:25:30,237 --> 00:25:31,238
[Karin] Mmm.

340
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:34,450
She said it out of nowhere
while we were eating.

341
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:38,495
And then she started speaking to him
in Korean, so I don't know what else…

342
00:25:38,579 --> 00:25:40,289
That was so rude of her.

343
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:42,833
I bet she brought that up on purpose
to bother you.

344
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:45,836
"We have a special connection,
and there's nothing you can do about it."

345
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:50,466
-You think so?
-Why else would she bring that up to you?

346
00:25:53,135 --> 00:25:54,219
Yeah, but…

347
00:25:55,054 --> 00:25:57,806
they looked like
they've known each other forever, and…

348
00:25:58,724 --> 00:25:59,725
It felt as if…

349
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:02,478
I was intruding on their conversation.

350
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:05,773
What? Karin, what are you saying?

351
00:26:05,856 --> 00:26:09,485
She's the one trying to come in between
you and Yubin. You know that.

352
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,528
Come between…

353
00:26:15,783 --> 00:26:17,451
You thought I couldn't tell?

354
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,745
Anybody with eyes can see it.

355
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:26,752
You and Yubin have
something special going on.

356
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:33,342
Karin, I noticed the warm way
Yubin looks and acts towards you.

357
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,928
He gets all awkward and kind of sweet.

358
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:40,099
But when he's around her,
he becomes someone else.

359
00:26:40,182 --> 00:26:42,017
Someone stern and cold.

360
00:26:42,101 --> 00:26:43,685
I mean, it was weird.

361
00:26:43,769 --> 00:26:47,022
The energy was so awkward and tense
that I had to leave.

362
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:50,776
Okay? Don't let her get to you.

363
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:03,664
Do you wanna know something fun?

364
00:27:04,248 --> 00:27:06,750
I'm gonna tell you
what scares her type the most.

365
00:27:07,668 --> 00:27:08,669
What is it?

366
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:12,339
Open up to her about how you feel.

367
00:27:13,257 --> 00:27:15,717
Face her directly and openly.

368
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:24,893
I don't really get it.

369
00:27:25,853 --> 00:27:26,937
Get what?

370
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:32,818
What if we…

371
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:38,740
Maybe Yubin and I were incompatible
from the very start.

372
00:27:40,242 --> 00:27:41,493
From the very start?

373
00:27:41,577 --> 00:27:43,745
Do you even know when that was, exactly?

374
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:46,290
Obstacles like
nationality, age, etcetera,

375
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:48,709
can all be overcome by honest love, right?

376
00:27:49,418 --> 00:27:54,381
What I'm not sure of is whether or not
Yubin is serious about a relationship.

377
00:27:55,048 --> 00:27:58,844
[sighs] And Sia is a lot more impressive
than me in every way.

378
00:28:02,848 --> 00:28:04,016
Remember the card I pulled?

379
00:28:05,851 --> 00:28:08,228
At the bus terminal
where you and Yubin met?

380
00:28:08,312 --> 00:28:10,480
Because I think it's about time
you pay attention to it.

381
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:14,860
It's the Wheel of Fortune.

382
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,446
It means you're bound
to have a fated encounter

383
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:20,073
camouflaged as a coincidence
in the near future.

384
00:28:23,827 --> 00:28:25,996
Mmm. I remember it.

385
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:28,248
If he appears before you
as if it were meant to be,

386
00:28:28,332 --> 00:28:29,708
maybe it's not a coincidence.

387
00:28:30,292 --> 00:28:33,378
But it's up to you to decide
whether he's the one for you or not.

388
00:28:34,338 --> 00:28:35,672
Is that a bad thing?

389
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:37,883
The outcome would be up to you.

390
00:28:38,634 --> 00:28:40,260
It's your choice.

391
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:43,180
Okay?

392
00:28:45,599 --> 00:28:47,267
Strawberries and romance.

393
00:28:47,768 --> 00:28:49,728
They're a lot more alike than you think.

394
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:53,774
The more love and care that you pour in,
the sweeter they get, right?

395
00:28:53,857 --> 00:28:55,442
So don't be afraid of it.

396
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:19,758
[in Korean] I'll think it over.

397
00:29:21,802 --> 00:29:22,844
Get home safe.

398
00:29:23,804 --> 00:29:24,805
I already missed my ferry.

399
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:27,307
What should I do?

400
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:29,267
How should I know?

401
00:29:29,351 --> 00:29:32,145
Let me stay with you.
I don't mind if we share a room.

402
00:29:32,229 --> 00:29:34,481
-Wait…
-[Mari] I have a place you can stay.

403
00:29:39,611 --> 00:29:41,279
-[Sia, in English] Oh, wait, wait…
-Bye!

404
00:29:42,823 --> 00:29:45,575
-[in Korean] Hey!
-[in English] Stop yappin' so much!

405
00:29:45,659 --> 00:29:48,286
Hey, young lady. You're way too loud.

406
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:56,670
Lay down and relax, dear.

407
00:29:57,212 --> 00:30:00,132
Don't pay us elder ladies any mind,
all right?

408
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,718
Have you eaten dinner yet?

409
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:05,345
Would you like me to make some soba?

410
00:30:17,858 --> 00:30:19,192
[Sia, in Korean] <i>It's all about timing.</i>

411
00:30:19,276 --> 00:30:20,694
Even as we speak,

412
00:30:20,777 --> 00:30:25,949
new competition is constantly emerging
to take your place, Lee Yubin.

413
00:30:27,117 --> 00:30:28,660
But you know that better than I do.

414
00:30:29,911 --> 00:30:33,040
I could get you on a new project
through some investors I know.

415
00:30:33,123 --> 00:30:36,668
Getting your name out there again?
It really isn't that hard, you know.

416
00:30:36,752 --> 00:30:39,212
Don't make it sound easy.

417
00:30:39,296 --> 00:30:40,505
But it is easy.

418
00:30:41,131 --> 00:30:44,760
You've got the talent,
and I've got the money.

419
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:47,721
As an entrepreneur,

420
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:50,223
I am here to make an offer

421
00:30:50,307 --> 00:30:52,893
to Lee Yubin, the spatial designer.

422
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:58,190
<i>I'm busy too. I won't wait around.</i>

423
00:31:13,789 --> 00:31:15,165
[in English] Hey, Yubin. Come here.

424
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:17,292
The sugar levels have finally risen.

425
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:18,710
-Look at that.
-[in Korean] Let's see.

426
00:31:19,252 --> 00:31:20,837
-[chuckles]
-Are you that happy?

427
00:31:20,921 --> 00:31:23,298
-So very happy! [chuckles]
-[chuckling]

428
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:30,388
[in English] Just trust me.

429
00:31:31,014 --> 00:31:33,767
-[chuckles]
-[cheers, laughs]

430
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:21,541
[in Korean] Did you see the photos?

431
00:33:22,542 --> 00:33:26,213
The view and the space
aren't bad, are they?

432
00:33:26,296 --> 00:33:30,091
We could just bulldoze over everything.

433
00:33:33,345 --> 00:33:34,596
Well, I'll see you in Korea.

434
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:47,442
-Karin, wait a second.
-Hmm?

435
00:33:48,193 --> 00:33:50,028
-Wear this.
-[in English] Uh…

436
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:51,321
You keep it, Yubin.

437
00:33:51,404 --> 00:33:53,073
No, you need to wear it.

438
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:54,908
-It's chilly.
-Mmm.

439
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:57,202
It's breezy. The wind is cold.

440
00:33:59,412 --> 00:34:00,664
-[in Korean] There.
-[Karin] Thank you.

441
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:02,666
What's with that smile?

442
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:09,673
[in English] Good morning, everybody.

443
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:12,801
Uh…

444
00:34:16,263 --> 00:34:17,639
Good morning.

445
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:21,851
How long are you planning on
staying with us, Sia?

446
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:24,187
I'm on my way out.

447
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:26,273
But I figured…

448
00:34:27,607 --> 00:34:29,025
while I'm here…

449
00:34:31,194 --> 00:34:33,863
Yubin and I could grab a coffee
before my ferry leaves.

450
00:34:33,947 --> 00:34:37,075
[in Korean] Hey, what are you doing?

451
00:34:43,665 --> 00:34:44,791
HYEJIN

452
00:34:51,298 --> 00:34:53,174
[Hyejin] <i>It's urgent. Pick up your phone.</i>

453
00:35:02,392 --> 00:35:05,854
[in English] Why don't we all just
grab a coffee together at Serendipity?

454
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:07,355
I'd love to treat you both.

455
00:35:07,856 --> 00:35:09,524
-[chuckles]
-[scoffs]

456
00:35:11,484 --> 00:35:12,611
Sure, why not?

457
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:16,281
There is actually something
I wanted to tell you anyway.

458
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,492
-[Yubin] Uh, Karin…
-Hmm?

459
00:35:19,576 --> 00:35:22,412
Um, why don't you two go on ahead?

460
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:25,624
I'll head over after my call.

461
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:28,668
-Mmm. Don't take too long.
-[Yubin] Okay.

462
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:35,258
[in Korean] You better leave
after you drink your coffee, okay?

463
00:35:35,342 --> 00:35:37,218
[in English] Mmm. Don't take too long.

464
00:35:52,776 --> 00:35:54,653
I set an alarm for when you need to leave.

465
00:35:54,736 --> 00:35:57,113
We wouldn't want you to miss your ferry
a second time, would we?

466
00:36:12,796 --> 00:36:13,797
All right, Sia.

467
00:36:15,799 --> 00:36:19,969
Tell me the real reason
that you came to Charo Island.

468
00:36:22,681 --> 00:36:27,686
I will. But first, I want you to tell me
how close you and Yubin really are.

469
00:36:27,769 --> 00:36:28,812
Sorry?

470
00:36:29,521 --> 00:36:31,106
How long have you known him?

471
00:36:32,941 --> 00:36:36,319
I've known Yubin
for almost an entire decade now.

472
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:43,243
Are you even aware
of the career Yubin had? How big he was?

473
00:36:47,372 --> 00:36:48,498
That's…

474
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:57,048
Karin, don't tell me that you don't
actually know why it is that he's here.

475
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:00,051
He told me…

476
00:37:01,094 --> 00:37:03,179
He ran into a bit of trouble in Korea

477
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:05,098
-so he needed to step away--
-He came to Charo Island

478
00:37:05,181 --> 00:37:06,766
because he wants to buy your land.

479
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:10,895
What?

480
00:37:11,396 --> 00:37:12,731
[in Korean] What are you talking about?

481
00:37:13,523 --> 00:37:15,525
[Hyejin] <i>Did you not know about this?</i>

482
00:37:15,608 --> 00:37:21,573
<i>I hear Sia is already negotiating</i>
<i>with the landowners around it.</i>

483
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:24,117
<i>They'll be done soon enough.</i>

484
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,828
<i>Even if you're unhappy</i>
<i>with the conditions and protest,</i>

485
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:30,248
<i>Sia plans to proceed</i>
<i>with the development of that area.</i>

486
00:37:30,331 --> 00:37:31,541
Okay, I understand.

487
00:37:32,459 --> 00:37:34,169
Thank you.

488
00:37:36,546 --> 00:37:40,216
Yubin is manipulating
and taking advantage of you, Karin.

489
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:43,636
All he wants from you is your property.

490
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:48,641
The sooner you stop being so stubborn,
he'll be able to return home.

491
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:51,561
Let him buy your plot of land already.

492
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:55,023
That way, he can get back to his future.

493
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:59,736
Shouldn't you sell Yubin your land?

494
00:38:01,821 --> 00:38:05,200
If you really care, help him get back
to where he belongs.

495
00:38:13,583 --> 00:38:15,168
[in Korean] Han Sia.

496
00:38:17,837 --> 00:38:18,838
We need to talk.

497
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:20,715
Why not.

498
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:34,729
What do you think you're doing?

499
00:38:36,773 --> 00:38:37,774
You heard?

500
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:40,151
What are you planning to do
with this village?

501
00:38:40,235 --> 00:38:42,654
-What's with that development plan?
-[door opens]

502
00:38:48,743 --> 00:38:52,413
[in English] Same as you, I'm here to
buy the land. Except, you came here first.

503
00:39:05,844 --> 00:39:08,096
-[in Korean] Stop playing games.
-You're the one who needs

504
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:09,639
-to stop playing games here.
-Han Sia.

505
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:12,433
I'm doing this with or without her land.

506
00:39:13,017 --> 00:39:16,020
I saw this place with my own eyes.

507
00:39:16,104 --> 00:39:19,148
There are many
who support this development.

508
00:39:20,316 --> 00:39:22,193
This project is happening
with or without you.

509
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:30,743
This is your last chance.

510
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:36,541
Leave already.

511
00:39:38,668 --> 00:39:39,919
If you walk away now,

512
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:43,131
your career is over.

513
00:39:59,981 --> 00:40:01,983
[Yubin] <i>I thought it might be</i>
<i>because of the strawberries.</i>

514
00:40:02,942 --> 00:40:05,320
I wanted to help out.

515
00:40:08,323 --> 00:40:13,411
I wanted to accurately represent
the field you work on

516
00:40:13,494 --> 00:40:16,164
and let everyone here see it.

517
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:18,333
Hmm. You can trust me.

518
00:40:29,719 --> 00:40:30,720
Wait.

519
00:40:31,846 --> 00:40:36,017
Karin, wait. Please hear me out.

520
00:40:38,144 --> 00:40:42,815
About earlier,
I don't want you to misunderstand.

521
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:48,696
[in English] You're not here
to buy my land?

522
00:40:51,741 --> 00:40:54,243
Ah, this… land?

523
00:40:55,411 --> 00:40:56,537
[in Korean] Right, all this…

524
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:58,206
It's true.

525
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:01,417
At first, I came to…

526
00:41:01,501 --> 00:41:02,794
You can't understand me.

527
00:41:04,921 --> 00:41:06,506
This land…

528
00:41:06,589 --> 00:41:09,968
Wait. Please, hear me out.

529
00:41:10,635 --> 00:41:15,890
I meant to explain all this to you…

530
00:41:23,731 --> 00:41:24,732
Hey, are you okay?

531
00:42:08,234 --> 00:42:09,485
[in English] Please…

532
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:13,531
I need you to leave.

533
00:42:14,866 --> 00:42:16,159
Get out of my house.

534
00:42:17,994 --> 00:42:19,454
Get off my land.

535
00:42:26,919 --> 00:42:28,296
But thank you…

536
00:42:30,757 --> 00:42:32,341
for everything.

537
00:43:15,301 --> 00:43:17,553
MERRY BERRY LOVE

538
00:43:17,637 --> 00:43:18,638
NEXT EPISODE

539
00:43:18,721 --> 00:43:20,973
[Sanggi, in Korean] <i>How did you end up</i>
<i>working for Sia's company?</i>

540
00:43:22,350 --> 00:43:25,770
[Mari, in English] <i>Splitting up,</i>
<i>it's a really hard thing to go through.</i>

541
00:43:26,521 --> 00:43:27,855
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>Karin.</i>

542
00:43:27,939 --> 00:43:29,023
<i>I care about you deeply.</i>
